@startuml redis_dji_worker_detail
title Redis and v2-dji-worker detail
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Frontend client" as Frontend
cloud "DJI cloud" as DJI

node "web container\nDjango ASGI" as Web {
  component "DjiMqttConsumer\n/ws/v2/dji/mqtt" as WsConsumer
  component "MQTT health API\nGET /api/v2/resource/dji-connections/mqtt-health" as HealthApi
  component "latest message API\nGET /api/v2/resource/dji-connections/{id}/mqtt-messages/latest" as LatestApi
}

node "v2-dji-worker container\npython manage.py run_v2_dji_worker" as Worker {
  component "connection loop\none thread per active DjiConnection" as ConnectionLoop
  component "workspace config\nget MQTT addr/user/password" as WorkspaceConfig
  component "MQTT subscriber\npaho client" as Subscriber
  component "message dispatcher\nhandle_message(topic, payload)" as Dispatcher
  component "periodic resource sync\nDJI_V2_RESOURCE_STATUS_SYNC_SECONDS" as ResourceSync
  component "periodic media sync\nDJI_V2_MEDIA_SYNC_SECONDS" as MediaSync
}

rectangle "Redis\nredis://redis:6379/0" as Redis {
  component "Channels layer\ngroup: v2.dji.mqtt" as ChannelLayer
  component "Heartbeat TTL keys\nv2:dji:mqtt:health:<connection_id>\nTTL: DJI_V2_MQTT_HEARTBEAT_TTL_SECONDS" as HeartbeatKeys
}

rectangle "PostgreSQL" as DB {
  component "v2_dji_connections" as DjiConnections
  component "v2_mqtt_connection_health" as MqttHealth
  component "v2_mqtt_latest_messages" as LatestMessages
  component "v2_drone_telemetry_snapshots" as Telemetry
  component "resource / mission / media tables" as BusinessTables
}

Frontend --> WsConsumer : subscribe with accessToken
WsConsumer --> ChannelLayer : group_add + receive mqtt.message

Frontend --> HealthApi : read worker health
HealthApi --> MqttHealth : persisted status
HealthApi --> HeartbeatKeys : volatile redisState

Frontend --> LatestApi : read last MQTT payloads
LatestApi --> LatestMessages : persisted latest messages

ConnectionLoop --> DjiConnections : load ACTIVE connections
ConnectionLoop --> WorkspaceConfig : per connection
WorkspaceConfig --> DJI : HTTP workspace config
WorkspaceConfig --> Subscriber : MQTT credentials
Subscriber --> DJI : subscribe topics\nosd/state/events/services_reply/status
Subscriber --> Dispatcher : on_message

Dispatcher --> LatestMessages : upsert latest by\nconnection + topic + deviceSn
Dispatcher --> MqttHealth : status/message_count/last_message_at
Dispatcher --> HeartbeatKeys : setex heartbeat
Dispatcher --> ChannelLayer : group_send envelope

Dispatcher --> Telemetry : /osd -> drone telemetry snapshot
Dispatcher --> BusinessTables : /status -> device status
Dispatcher --> BusinessTables : /events or /services_reply\n-> mission execution status

ConnectionLoop --> ResourceSync : interval sync
ResourceSync --> DJI : discover/status HTTP
ResourceSync --> BusinessTables : update resources/bindings

ConnectionLoop --> MediaSync : interval sync
MediaSync --> DJI : media list/download URL refresh
MediaSync --> BusinessTables : update cloud media sync state

note right of Redis
Redis does not store business truth.
It is only:
1. cross-process WebSocket broadcast
2. short-lived worker heartbeat
end note

note bottom of Worker
run_once: resource sync + due media sync, then exit.
run_forever: connect MQTT, process messages, and run periodic sync loops.
end note

@enduml
